#14757
The Altar of Xerxes~
Under the crimson illumination of glowing eyes in the walls, sits an Altar
of black marble. Ribbons of gold writhe throu the marble like veins in a dying
mans body. No stain of blood or stench of death is upon it, but yet you
feel as if no place you have ever known seemed so horrible. Here, vile rites
of worship to abominable to fathom have taken place. While clean, the altar
seems none the less tainted by the terrible suffering and hideous evil that
has taken place upon it. You see one item sits upon the altar, a dark orb
that seems even blacker than the altar itself. To the south lies a marble
door, while lines of sablewood pews stretch out to the west.
~
