#14758
Vestry~
The walls, ceiling and floor of this chamber are of a lustrous black marble,
gold-veins glimmering on it's surface. Set into the wall is a closet of
sablewood, almost as black as the marble itself. The room is lit by sconces
in the wall in which balls of incense burn slowly, giving off a dim light.
An ornate arch-way is carved into the northern wall, beyond you can see lines
of pews in what is clearly some unholy place of worship. You feel reluctant
to pass through the arch, indeed, the open marble door to the west leads to
safety, take it while you can.
~
