similiar black marble to the Chapel outside, althou here, hundreds of gem
stones are set into the ceiling, glittering like baleful demonic eyes as light
strikes them. In the four corners of the room, tall candles of tallow gutter
sporadically. These illuminate a large bed in the centre of the room, beside
which lies a full-length mirror and a small table upon which rests obsidian
goblets containing some red liquid. A door of marble in the north wall leads
to the Chapel.
